", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "1a5bf65b0f8900dd5218c92e709798ee7f7e53ea", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 288111800}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1a5bf65b0f8900dd5218c92e709798ee7f7e53ea", "title": "SCALAR: Self-Supervised Composition and Learning of Skills with LLM Planning and RL", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "bd215b5308ea85fa6fa37e669c48ae13be7ddcb4", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 288702210}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/bd215b5308ea85fa6fa37e669c48ae13be7ddcb4", "title": "ReflexGrad: A Dual-Process Architecture for Gradient-Free Inference-Time Learning", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "51310265", "name": "Ankush D. Kadu"}, {"authorId": "2386523184", "name": "Ashwanth Krishnan"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "ad8190f0d99144852eaa2b5d13c1fe71a6f14ab7", "externalIds": {"DOI": "10.29007/8fsx", "CorpusId": 287621613}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/ad8190f0d99144852eaa2b5d13c1fe71a6f14ab7", "title": "Agentic Knowledge Graph Traversal in Protein-Protein Relation Grounding", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null, "disclaimer": "Notice: Paper or abstract available at https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/10.29007/8fsx?email=<INSERT_YOUR_EMAIL> or https://doi.org/10.29007/8fsx, which is subject to the license by the author or copyright owner provided with this content. Please go to the source to verify the license and copyright information for your use."}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2294721250", "name": "Gabriel Reder"}, {"authorId": "2055820126", "name": "Charles C Collins"}, {"authorId": "2316487025", "name": "Larisa N. Soldatova"}, {"authorId": "2257167844", "name": "Ross D. King"}], "abstract": "Automated semantic knowledge extraction from scientific literature promises to open vast quantities of scientific knowledge to formal analysis and computationally-driven discovery. In this work we investigate the promise of Large Language Model (LLM) agents in extracting structured knowledge from biomedical texts, specifically for grounding protein-protein interaction (PPI) relations to terms in the PSI-MI ontology of molecular interactions. While LLMs excel at summarization, they struggle to interface with structured knowledge representations. We equipped agents with various knowledge graph interaction strategies and measured their PPI grounding performance. Our central finding is that PageRank-guided traversal, a method rooted in graph topology, consistently outperforms embedding-based approaches such as retrieval augmented generation (RAG) and top-down traversal strategies including breadth-first search (BFS), depth-first search (DFS), and local greedy search in extracting knowledge previously missed by human curators. Our initial results indicate that the structure of a well-curated knowledge base is itself a powerful source of information, an underutilized principle in current agentic knowledge base interaction methods."}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "1f53e8e7f3b7cda77f99811ed5f277b5f700dca2", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 289334674}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1f53e8e7f3b7cda77f99811ed5f277b5f700dca2", "title": "A Self-Aware BDI Agent for LLM-Driven Reasoning: Architecture, Design, and Preliminary Evaluation", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "120102199", "name": "C. Lawton"}, {"authorId": "30509765", "name": "D. Sacharny"}, {"authorId": "2210749330", "name": "T. C. Henderson"}, {"authorId": "2259295504", "name": "Tom Henderson"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "f0a3410eb24f296bb5f9f35e24c2f5ce7a6d0580", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 289553124}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/f0a3410eb24f296bb5f9f35e24c2f5ce7a6d0580", "title": "VeriBench: An End-to-End Formal Verification Benchmark for AI Coding Agents in Lean 4", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "e04808bd42736d00e5f2a46fa9e687055d2afb88", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 289941488}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/e04808bd42736d00e5f2a46fa9e687055d2afb88", "title": "Agent Step Value: State-Transition Measurement with State-Grounded LLM Evaluators", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2448023764", "name": "Andrew Zhang"}, {"authorId": "2448107431", "name": "Cheng-Zhan Li"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "3955740761807c76d62f9eb3f35b4eb713c7f7be", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 289934537}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/3955740761807c76d62f9eb3f35b4eb713c7f7be", "title": "Agent Step Value: Probing the Observer Effect in Black-Box Traces", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [{"authorId": "2448023764", "name": "Andrew Zhang"}, {"authorId": "2448107431", "name": "Cheng-Zhan Li"}], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "64da2ef35237dc2635415920241578d9b0b03ce1", "externalIds": {"CorpusId": 289983099}, "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/64da2ef35237dc2635415920241578d9b0b03ce1", "title": "Autonomous Agent Learning in Production", "openAccessPdf": {"url": "", "status": null, "license": null}, "fieldsOfStudy": null, "publicationDate": null, "authors": [], "abstract": null}}, {"citingPaper": {"paperId": "131522f8710a552228e5497df9df1c